    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0425" n="396" xml:id="pg396"/>

                <head>144. Memorandum From Secretary of State Acheson and the Director for Mutual
                    Security (Harriman) to the Executive Secretary of the National Security Council
                        (Lay)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d144-f1"/></head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1953-01-19">January 19, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Sixth Progress Report on NSC 104/2, “U.S. Policies and Programs in the
                        Economic Field which may Affect the War Potential of the Soviet Bloc”<anchor
                            n="2" xml:id="d144-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>REFERENCES</head>
                    <label>A.</label>
                    <item>NSC 104/2</item>
                    <label>B.</label>
                    <item>Memorandum for NSC from Executive Secretary, “Assignment of
                        Responsibilities for Economic Defense”, dated November 7, 1951,<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d144-f3"/> transmitting Memorandum by the President on this
                        subject</item>
                    <label>C.</label>
                    <item>Memorandum for NSC from Executive Secretary, “Assignment of
                        Responsibilities for Economic Defense”, dated January 25, 1952<anchor n="4"
                            xml:id="d144-f4"/> transmitting Memorandum of Agreement between the
                        Secretary of State and the Administrator of the Mutual Defense Assistance
                        Control Act</item>
                </list>
                <p>In accordance with the President’s directive on the assignment of
                    responsibilities for economic defense under NSC 104/2 and the memorandum of
                    agreement between the Secretary of State and the Administrator of the Mutual
                    Defense Assistance Control Act, there is submitted herewith the sixth progress
                    report on NSC 104/2.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d144-f5"/> It is requested that this
                    be circulated to the members of the Council for their information.</p>
                <closer><signed>Dean Acheson</signed><anchor n="6" xml:id="d144-f6"/></closer>


                <xi:include href="d144-a1.xml" xpointer="d144-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d144-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d144-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, S/S–NSC Files: Lot 63 D 351, OCB Files, NSC
                    104, Memoranda 1952–53, Box 61. Secret; Security Information. A handwritten
                    notation on the memorandum indicates that it was delivered to Lay at the NSC on
                    January 19 by security messenger.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f2" n="2" xml:id="d144-f2-content">
                <p>NSC 104/2 is printed in <ref target="frus1951v01#pg_1059"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Foreign Relations</hi>, 1951, vol. I, pp. 1059</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1951v01#pg_1064">1064</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f3" n="3" xml:id="d144-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d116-f4">footnote 4, Document 116</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f4" n="4" xml:id="d144-f4-content">
                <p>Ibid.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f5" n="5" xml:id="d144-f5-content">
                <p>The 24-page progress report and Appendix 1, Replies from COCOM Countries on Prior
                    Commitments Issue, are attached but not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f6" n="6" xml:id="d144-f6-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature. The signature block for the
                    Director of Mutual Security is blank.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
